## Is It the Acrylic or the Process That Damages Your Nails?

Most people assume the acrylic material is doing the damage. It isn't. Acrylic, once cured, is chemically inert against the nail plate. <strong>Do acrylic nails damage your nails</strong> by sitting there? No. The damage comes from two moments: how aggressively the nail was filed before the acrylic went on, and how the set was removed afterward.

Think of the acrylic as a shell, not a treatment. A shell doesn't hurt what's underneath unless someone forces their way through it, which is exactly what over-filing and prying do.

This is why two people can wear the same acrylic brand for years with different outcomes. One has a tech who files conservatively and soaks the product off. The other has had sets pried off more than once. Same acrylic. Different nails.

