## How Long It Takes Nails to Recover From Acrylic Damage

Mild thinning grows out within a few weeks. Moderate damage, ridges, brittleness, visible peeling, generally takes four to eight weeks of consistent care. Full recovery from deeper damage, including onycholysis or significant plate thinning, tracks the full nail growth cycle: roughly three to six months from cuticle to tip. However long <strong>do acrylic nails damage your nails</strong> takes to reverse in your case, the timeline depends on depth, not on how the acrylic was formulated.

That range isn't vague reassurance, it's just how nails work. A fingernail grows about three millimetres a month, and it doesn't heal in place, it grows out. Whatever section was thinned or separated has to travel the full length of the nail before it's gone.

The timeline is predictable and shorter than most people brace for. Weeks one and two look the roughest. By weeks three and four, new growth at the base is visibly stronger. By months three to four, most people are back to baseline. Consistent hydration and a real break from enhancements make the biggest difference. The <a href='https://mirelleinspo.com/blog/nail-strengthening/diy-nail-strengthening-treatments-at-home'>DIY nail strengthening treatments to speed up recovery</a> guide covers what actually helps.

